<UserControl x:Class="TcXunit.Vsix.ResultsToolWindowControl"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:wv2="clr-namespace:Microsoft.Web.WebView2.Wpf;assembly=Microsoft.Web.WebView2.Wpf"
             mc:Ignorable="d"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             d:DesignHeight="400" d:DesignWidth="350">
    <!--
      Row 1 (the former WPF TreeView) is now a WebView2 loading Resources/results.html,
      which itself loads vsix-tokens.css/vsix-shell.css/results.css; see
      docs/design-system.html section 8 and TcXunit-1tt.1. Results-tree rendering into
      the WebView2 is TcXunit-1tt.2. WebView2 fills its row edge-to-edge (no Margin) so
      the panel's own dark chrome reaches the tool window's borders, matching
      TcAgentPlugin's chat panel.

      TcXunit-1tt.3 retires the native WPF "Run tests (tcxunit)" Button that used to sit
      in Row 0: docs/design-system.html's toolbar has exactly one primary action
      (.send-btn, toggling to .stop-btn while a run is in flight, per its "exactly two
      buttons" rule and user story 12's "unambiguous about which action is live") and
      that now lives entirely inside the WebView2 page as #runButton (results.html),
      driven by ResultsToolWindowControl.xaml.cs's StartRunAsync/StopRun over
      window.chrome.webview.postMessage / CoreWebView2.WebMessageReceived. StatusText
      remains as a host-level fallback for errors the WebView2 page itself can't show
      (e.g. WebView2 failing to initialize, tcxunit.json missing); everything else
      (running state, run results) is pushed into the page. Note: this comment avoids
      the double-hyphen aside this codebase otherwise favors in .cs/.js/.css files,
      since XML comments may not contain one; semicolons/parens stand in instead.
    -->
    <Grid>
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" x:Name="StatusText" Margin="8,8,8,8" TextWrapping="Wrap" Visibility="Collapsed" />

        <wv2:WebView2 Grid.Row="1" x:Name="Browser" />
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
